      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve taken the two jars, unzipped them, selected the common .class files and ran this script:\n```\nfind before_jar/ -name \u0027*.class\u0027 | sort | sed \u0027s/^before_jar\\///\u0027 \u003e before.txt\nfind after_jar/  -name \u0027*.class\u0027 | sort | sed \u0027s/^after_jar\\///\u0027  \u003e after.txt\n\necho \u0027Diff between jars\u0027\ndiff before.txt after.txt\n\necho \u0027javap diffs\u0027\necho \u0027\u0027\ncommon_files\u003d$(cat after.txt)\ntotal\u003d$(wc -l \u003c after.txt)\nprocessed\u003d0\nargs\u003d\u0027-v -s -p -constants\u0027\nfor i in $common_files;\ndo\n    processed\u003d$((processed + 1))\n    echo -ne \u0027\\r\u0027\n    echo -ne \"$processed/$total\"\n    diff \u003c(javap $args before_jar/$i | sed \u0027s/^Classfile .*$//\u0027 | sed \u0027s/Last modified.*$//\u0027) \u003c(javap $args after_jar/$i| sed \u0027s/^Classfile .*$//\u0027 | sed \u0027s/Last modified.*$//\u0027) \u0026\ndone\necho \u0027\u0027\n```\nI ran this on the jar in the S branch, and got 0 diffs using javap for the common .class files.",
